      "text": "In the Pearl of Great Price, the Book of Mormon, God said, \"Worlds Without Numbers Have I Created.\" Moses, however, was shown only the world and its inhabitants which are and were created upon which he stood.\"\n\nNote that two (2) verbs are used here: are and were. Are refers to our current generation and its civilization; whereas, were refers to the many many ancient generations and its civilizations before us us now being discovered by archaeologists. In addition, it claims that there are many Adams and Eves.\n\nComparatively, in the book Conversations With God, the Almighty Creator said, \" We only repeat history.\"",
